    "notes": "Native opposite source pairs and the actual live capture sequence show projection drift: frames 0..2 have a foreshortened thicker rifle/fore-end, while 3..5 lengthen and flatten the rifle with a more side-on torso. Frame4 in particular lifts the muzzle relative to the head, and frame5 changes visible magazine/fore-end projection. The 2-to-3 and 5-to-0 connections need source continuity repair, not speed changes or limb warps. New two-leg anatomy remains a source-level improvement but does not approve whole-cycle weapon/body continuity.",
